55: 
56: Preserve all other bytes/files, BOM, XML declaration, tabs, LF, entity spelling, ordering, final newline and `Bld_autoIncrement=true`; no resave or metadata exception. Keep the complete original and MIT notice immutable outside writable arms, hash before/after, and retain complete edited bytes, file/dependency inventories, original/output source map, raw failures and accounting. Root `LVVersion=20008000` is a declaration only; WP1 original `save_version` remains unavailable. Neither that declaration nor the build-version property supplies native save-version authority, build behavior or WB1's source/build chain.
57: 
58: The distinct `project_text` controls derive in-memory byte fixtures from the pinned original. One positive and 30 fixed rejecting controls check no-op, wrong locator/value/precondition/original/allowance, unrelated bytes/files, missing/extra output, original overwrite, BOM/declaration/line-ending/entity/final-newline rewrites, duplicate locator, wrong property type, root-version drift and unsupported native/dependency/build/behavior/save-version/overall passes. Four of those controls also reject promoting the root declaration to native save version, inventing a native key or overall pass, and dropping WP1 from the method inventory. Exact inventory and reasons are asserted independently of the fixture list. The existing 44 synthetic rejections remain unchanged. No edited project is emitted and these examples are no trial.
59: 
60: WP1 text and root-declaration trial results remain `unexecuted`; native validity, dependencies, build and behavior remain `unexecuted`; native save version and overall writing remain `unverified`. A positive preparation fixture supplies neither an answer scorer nor an overall writing pass. C1 remains open: structured controls and integrity hashes do not establish arbitrary narrative or future answers; independent semantic, extra-claim, contradiction and original/output citation review remains required.
61: 
